-- observations_1d: 1 day buckets, read from observations_1h.
--
-- Three properties of this file are not negotiable, are easy to get wrong, and are
-- silent when wrong. They are properties of the generator's template, not of
-- whoever called it:
--
--   * sums accumulate in double precision, never in the column's own type. `sum(real)`
--     returns `real`, float4 addition is not associative, and a hierarchy therefore
--     adds in a different order than a direct scan — measured wrong in 55 of 56
--     uneven-bucket pairs, bit-identical in 56 of 56 once widened (D-14).
--   * counts are nulled at zero. `count()` returns 0 and never NULL, so on a
--     70%-NULL table a plain count column is fully populated and almost entirely
--     zeroes — 347 MB against 234 MB on a 398-column month (D-16).
--   * no column holds a finished average, and this level reads 1h rather than raw.
